<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns BBB pi ratings to nine Japan companies.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns BBB pi ratings to nine Japan companies.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's (S&amp;P) said on Tuesday it had assigned its &quot;BBB&quot; public information (pi) rating to nine Japanese companies and its &quot;BB&quot; pi rating to nine others.</p>
<p>It said it had assigned its &quot;A&quot; rating to two Japanese firms.</p>
<p>S&amp;P says its pi ratings are arrived at by employing similar analytical procedures to those used to make traditional credit ratings but are based on public disclosure and other sources of information.  </p>
<p>S&amp;P also said it had assigned its &quot;B&quot; pi rating to one Japanese firm.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said that it had assigned its pi ratings to a total of 21 Japanese companies in the oil, steel, glass, high-technology, airline and general merchandise industries.</p>
<p>The ratings are as follows:</p>
<p>    Oil industry     General Sekiyu KK     BBBpi</p>
<p>			   Mitsubishi Oil Co Ltd BBBpi</p>
<p>			   Nippon Oil Co Ltd     BBBpi</p>
<p>			   Showa Shell Sekiyu KK BBBpi</p>
<p>			   Cosmo Oil Co Ltd	 BBpi</p>
<p>			   Japan Energy Corp	 Bpi</p>
<p>    Steel		Nippon Steel Corp     BBBpi</p>
<p>			   Kawasaki Steel Corp    BBpi</p>
<p>			   Kobe Steel Ltd	   BBpi</p>
<p>			   NKK Corp		   BBpi</p>
<p>			   Sumitomo Metal Ind Ltd BBpi</p>
<p>    Glass		Central Glass Co Ltd  BBBpi</p>
<p>			   Nippon Sheet Glass Co BBBpi</p>
<p>    High-tech	  Fujitsu Ltd		 Api</p>
<p>			   Oki Electric Ind Co   BBBpi</p>
<p>Airline industry     All Nippon Airways Co BBBpi</p>
<p>			   Japan Air System Co    BBpi</p>
<p>General Merchandise Industry</p>
<p>			   Jusco Co Ltd		Api</p>
<p>			   Daiei Inc		  BBpi</p>
<p>			   Mycal Corp		 BBpi</p>
<p>			   Seiyu Ltd		  BBpi</p>
<p>&quot;In conducting our review of Japanese corporate borrowers, S&amp;P's pi ratings represent a strong commitment to balancing the interests of all market participants, investors and issuers,&quot; Edward Z. Emmer, S&amp;P's executive managing director of corporate ratings, said in a statement.</p>
</text>
